{
 "slug": "js_temporal_mistakes",
 "course": "js",
 "order": 198,
 "url": "/js/js_temporal_mistakes.asp",
 "title": "JavaScript Temporal Mistakes",
 "blocks": [
  {
   "type": "h1",
   "text": "JavaScript Temporal Mistakes"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Temporal is a powerful API, but it can be confusing at first."
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "ordered": false,
   "items": [
    "Remember to use the correct Temporal type",
    "Avoid implicit conversions",
    "Always handle time zones correctly",
    "Use compare() instead of < and >",
    "Remember that Temporal Objects are immutable"
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Here are some common mistakes and how to avoid them."
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Missing UTC (Z) for Instant"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "An Instant must always include UTC."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "const instant = Temporal.Instant.from(\"2026-05-17T14:30:00\");",
   "caption": "Wrong"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "const instant = Temporal.Instant.from(\"2026-05-17T14:30:00Z\");",
   "caption": "Wrong"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_temporal_error_instant"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Using PlainDateTime with Time Zone"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "PlainDateTime does not support time zones."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "const date = Temporal.PlainDateTime.from(\"2026-05-17T14:30:00Z\");",
   "caption": "Wrong"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "const date = Temporal.ZonedDateTime.from(\"2026-05-17T14:30:00\");",
   "caption": "Wrong"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_temporal_error_plaindatetime"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Comparing Different Types"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Temporals can go wrong when comparing different types."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "const d1 = Temporal.PlainDate.from(\"2026-05-17\");\n\nconst d2 = Temporal.Instant.from(\"2026-05-17T14:30Z\");\n\nTemporal.PlainDate.compare(d1, d2);",
   "caption": "Wrong"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_temporal_error_compare"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "const d1 = Temporal.PlainDate.from(\"2026-05-17\");\n\nconst d2 = Temporal.PlainDateTime.from(\"2026-05-17T14:30\");\n\nTemporal.PlainDate.compare(d1, d2);",
   "caption": "Correct"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_temporal_error_compare_ok"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Using equals() with Different Types"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Temporals can go wrong when comparing different types."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "const d1 = Temporal.PlainDate.from(\"2026-05-17\");\n\nconst d2 = Temporal.Instant.from(\"2026-05-17T14:30Z\");\n\nd1.equals(d2);",
   "caption": "Wrong"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_temporal_error_equals"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "const d1 = Temporal.PlainDate.from(\"2026-05-17\");\n\nconst d2 = Temporal.PlainDateTime.from(\"2026-05-17T14:30\");\n\nd1.equals(d2.toPlainDate());",
   "caption": "Correct"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_temporal_error_equals_ok"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Using ==, < or > for Comparison"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Temporal objects cannot be compared with ==, ===, < or >."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "const d1 = Temporal.PlainDate.from(\"2026-05-17\");\n\nconst d2 = Temporal.PlainDate.from(\"2026-05-17\");\n\nd1 === d2; // False\n\nd1 == d2;  // False\n\nd1 < d2;   // TypeError\n\nd1 > d2;   // TypeError",
   "caption": "Wrong"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "const d1 = Temporal.PlainDate.from(\"2026-05-17\");\n\nconst d2 = Temporal.PlainDate.from(\"2026-05-17\");\n\nTemporal.PlainDate.compare(d1, d2);",
   "caption": "Wrong"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_temporal_error_less_than"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Expecting Mutation"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Temporal objects are immutable."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "const date = Temporal.PlainDate.from(\"2026-05-17\");\n\ndate.add({ months: 1 });",
   "caption": "Wrong"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "const date = Temporal.PlainDate.from(\"2026-05-17\");\n\nconst next = d.add({ months: 1 });",
   "caption": "Wrong"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_temporal_error_mutation"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Using valueOf()"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Temporal objects do not convert to numbers."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "const date = Temporal.PlainDate.from(\"2026-05-17\");\n\ntry {\n\n  text = date.valueOf();\n\n} catch (err) {\n\n  text = err.name;\n\n}",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_temporal_error_valueof"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Using Instant for Local Time"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Instant is always UTC (not local time)."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "Temporal.Now.instant(); // not local time",
   "caption": "Wrong"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "Temporal.Now.zonedDateTimeISO();",
   "caption": "Wrong"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_temporal_error_local"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Using PlainDate for Time"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "PlainDate has no time."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "Temporal.PlainDate.from(\"2026-05-17T14:30\");",
   "caption": "Wrong"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "Temporal.PlainDateTime.from(\"2026-05-17T14:30\");",
   "caption": "Wrong"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_temporal_error_plaindate"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Forgetting Time Zone in ZonedDateTime"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "ZonedDateTime requires a time zone."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "Temporal.ZonedDateTime.from(\"2026-05-17T14:30:00\");",
   "caption": "Wrong"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_temporal_error_zoned"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "Temporal.ZonedDateTime.from(\"2026-05-17T14:30:00+02:00[Europe/Oslo]\");",
   "caption": "Correct"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_temporal_error_zoned_ok"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Not Choosing the Right Type"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Each Temporal type has a specific purpose."
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [],
   "rows": [
    [
     "Type",
     "Use"
    ],
    [
     "Instant",
     "Exact moment (UTC)"
    ],
    [
     "PlainDate",
     "Date only"
    ],
    [
     "PlainTime",
     "Time only"
    ],
    [
     "PlainDateTime",
     "Date + time only"
    ],
    [
     "ZonedDateTime",
     "Date + time + time zone"
    ],
    [
     "Duration",
     "Length of time only"
    ]
   ]
  }
 ]
}